WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.350
There’s English bread, German bread, and French bread,

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:07.230
but Japan’s bread, <i>Japan</i>, does not exist.

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.570
In that case, there’s no choice but to create it.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:12.900
This story is a serious, biographical ballad of a boy who possesses Solar Hands,

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:18.160
Azuma Kazuma, who will create a Japanese bread made by and for the Japanese people,

00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.750
which can be presented to the world proudly.

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:39.060
Somewhere far away, there are people listening carefully.

00:00:40.390 --> 00:00:47.030
In every place, there are people looking up at the sky.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:54.910
Under the night sky, we, who are whistling...

00:00:55.950 --> 00:01:02.620
without words, are just tracing constellations with our fingers.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:10.090
The dreams of the cold-sensitive... Your cold hands...

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:19.470
The warming magic is to believe in one path.

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:28.230
The single star found on the other side of the comet cloud...

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:32.490
whether it be a shining or a faint star...

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:35.450
is the light of only you.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.230
On the other side of the cloud in your heart,

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:44.040
is a sign post that remains unseen.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:51.760
Now, opening these hands, what will you believe in today?

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.880
Kazuma disqualified!?

00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:58.020
Resurrection from the brink of death by Ultra C!

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:00.930
According to your present grades,

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:05.480
the 16 people who chose G and the 13
people who chose A add up to 29.

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.440
And, including the Main Branch employee Suwabara,

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:11.400
30 people have attained the right to the finals.

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.610
Regulations require 32. The other 2 will be
selected after sampling their food items.

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:16.150
What’s with 30 people being selected
without their rolls being sampled?
Regulations require 32. The other 2 will be
selected after sampling their food items.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.150
There’s only 2 more after this, right?

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:18.990
So strict!

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:20.700
Before that,

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:22.500
the 13 people who chose C...

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:23.990
That’s me!

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:25.750
It’s us.

00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:28.620
I judge you to be TRASH!

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:30.620
Eh? Trash?

00:02:30.620 --> 00:02:32.500
All of you are disqualified!

00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:33.880
Disqualified
All of you are disqualified!

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.340
Disqualified?

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.090
Azuma is... disqualified?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:42.220
W-Why?

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:44.100
Why are we disqualified?

00:02:45.310 --> 00:02:48.350
Very well.
Let me tell you what C was!

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:51.060
It was margarine, you idiot!

00:02:51.060 --> 00:02:54.110
Trash like you who can’t even figure the
difference between margarine and butter

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.360
are not even worth talking about.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:57.400
Margarine?

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:58.400
That’s a lie, isn’t it?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.700
Don’t mess with us!

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.610
Is that fair?

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:06.240
Believing in you, we selected C and still...

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:08.040
What are you going to do about this, huh?

00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:09.830
Dammit!

00:03:09.830 --> 00:03:10.960
What are you talking about?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.580
Don’t play innocent.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.330
Apologize!

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:16.420
Come on!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.800
W-Why?

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.770
Stand back.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.140
Stand back, you vomit!

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.640
Scary!

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.720
That rotten spirit of yours,

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:29.100
to depend on another’s choice instead
of your own strength...

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.350
it makes me want to puke!

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:34.230
In addition, if the choice made is
wrong, then it’s his fault, is it?

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:35.780
Learn some shame!

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:41.320
Please spare my life, at least.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:44.200
And, Kuroyanagi...

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:46.330
An artisan of your level,

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:49.120
not noticing Azuma’s “Ultra C,”
which reversed the

00:03:49.120 --> 00:03:51.210
handicap he had when he chose C...

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:52.540
What did you say?

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:56.290
Oh? Very impressive, Suwabara.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.380
He’s seen the miracle that Azuma has created.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.010
“The miracle that Azuma has created?”

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.100
In order to create an excellent sword,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.820
it’s not just about selecting good steel.

00:04:12.730 --> 00:04:16.150
The delicate conditions while
forging it are also important.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:19.030
Conditions while forging?

00:04:19.030 --> 00:04:20.190
You still don’t get it?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:21.950
At that time...

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:25.580
Azuma chose the margarine and made the dough...

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:30.170
and finished baking the bread in 3 minutes,
almost like he’d given up on the challenge.

00:04:31.750 --> 00:04:33.170
It’s a good fragrance.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:34.460
3 minutes!

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.670
D-Don’t tell me...

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.550
Azuma, hand over your bread.

00:04:38.550 --> 00:04:40.250
What are you getting mad about?

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:41.880
Never mind that and
hand it over, will you?

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.900
T-This is...

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.360
This is...

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:00.780
Vapor action!

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.440
Ac-choon! Ac-choon!

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.570
Kuroyanagi-san’s birthday is...

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.700
Ac-choon! Ac-choon! Ac-choon!

00:05:08.700 --> 00:05:11.290
Annoying!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.410
Not paper, but vapor!

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:14.880
Paper
Vapor
Not paper, but vapor!

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:15.660
Vapor
Paper

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.460
What’s “vapor action?”

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:21.170
Rather than that, who were you talking to, Kuroyanagi?

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.460
What?

00:05:22.460 --> 00:05:24.170
What in the world is “vapor action?”

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:27.260
To not even know what vapor action is...

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:28.890
Well then, let me tell you.

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:29.890
Listen well.

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.190
The butter roll is normally baked for about
15 minutes at a temperature of

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:37.650
less than 200°C.

00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:41.110
But if you expose it to a super high temperature of over

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:43.740
300°C for the short period of 3 minutes,

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:46.360
you would make the water content within
the bread dough explode instantly,

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:48.280
causing the bread to puff up and be done.

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.080
That is vapor action.

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.870
At a glance, the logic appears to be simple,

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:56.710
but baking it at such high temperatures
is the worst for an artisan.

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:58.920
You’re back to back with the possibility of burning it,

00:05:58.920 --> 00:06:02.000
and going just 3 seconds over the time
period would result in burning it.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:07.130
The timing is so difficult that only a first
class baker can handle this technique.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.180
Where in the world did you learn such a technique?

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:14.220
Um... the butter roll of my school lunch
in primary school wasn’t very tasty.

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:18.100
So I tried various improvements.

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:20.730
And then, this happened some way or another, but...

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.440
was it all that great a thing?

00:06:23.690 --> 00:06:25.440
“Some way or another,” he says...

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:30.160
To have not just the <i>Japan</i> up his sleeve,
but such techniques as well...

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:31.950
I really can’t underestimate this guy.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.910
Kuroyanagi.

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:39.120
Azuma Kazuma’s disqualification
is withdrawn as a special case.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:40.960
You’ve passed the preliminary.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:41.880
Is that all right?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.210
Hey, wait one moment!

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:44.630
Like we could be satisfied with that!

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:46.920
You can’t call it a butter roll if it has margarine in it!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:51.550
Anything other than A, G, and E
are snotty or trashy butters!

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:53.260
There can’t be much of a difference with it.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:55.100
But, with margarine, it’s...

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.480
Sample the others as well!

00:06:56.480 --> 00:06:58.060
Shut up!

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:01.610
Then, I’ll give a chance to the others
who’ve selected C as well.

00:07:01.610 --> 00:07:05.700
Decide who the last person will be amongst
the remaining 27 via rock-paper-scissors.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.820
Rock-paper-scissors?

00:07:07.820 --> 00:07:08.900
Don’t mess with us!

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:09.900
What are you thinking?

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:11.530
Hey, all you trash.

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:14.490
You’re all the same level as garbage and crap.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:17.200
It’s better to choose someone
who at least has good luck.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:19.960
As usual, he’s out of the ordinary.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:21.750
And in one sense,
he’s extraordinarily stupid.

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:26.550
You can say anything.

00:07:26.550 --> 00:07:27.960
After eating that tasty a butter rol–

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:30.430
no, margarine roll,

00:07:30.430 --> 00:07:33.050
I don’t want to sully my mouth with your trash breads.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:37.390
The announcement of the drawing of
your names for the finals is at 3:00.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:40.520
All of you who’ve passed should
stand by around the hall.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:43.440
Again, the finals will start tomorrow at noon.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.610
That’s all. Disperse.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:47.780
It can’t be helped.

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:48.990
Shall we do rock-paper-scissors?

00:07:49.650 --> 00:07:51.110
It’s rock first, right?

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:54.320
I was afraid for a moment as to what would happen.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:55.670
Tsukino.

00:07:56.200 --> 00:07:56.960
Yes?

00:07:57.660 --> 00:07:59.960
That tomboy of a girl passed as well, didn’t she?

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.340
It appears as if there really is
no choice but to fight it out.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:18.850
Sooner or later, it’s a route that
we’ll have to take someday.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:22.190
All right!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:23.730
I’ll be working hard from tomorrow.

00:08:23.730 --> 00:08:25.190
Hey, you...

00:08:25.190 --> 00:08:26.110
You’re amazing, aren’t you?

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.610
You passed, even though you made something that’s different from the theme.

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:30.230
Huh? Who are you?

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:31.780
Me?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.700
I’m Mizuno.
Of the New Tokyo Branch.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.410
Mizuno?

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:37.950
By Mizuno, you mean that...

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.960
Movies are really good things...

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:54.010
You have the same name as Haruo-sensei,
whom I really admire.

00:08:54.010 --> 00:08:56.180
Would you happen to be related?

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.310
Huh? Haruo-sensei?

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.560
No, no...

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:07.940
I’m Azusagawa Mizuno, of the New Tokyo Branch.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:10.440
Azuma Kazuma-kun, you’re really interesting!

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.450
W-Why do you know my name?

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:15.700
That’s obvious.

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.950
Azuma Kazuma-kun, of the Southern Tokyo Branch.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.330
I can’t possibly not know you, someone
who’s even appeared on TV.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:23.200
You’re a person to be watched out for.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:30.800
You’re heavy, so don’t hug me!

00:09:30.800 --> 00:09:32.550
They’re beginning to get friendly, aren’t they?

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.180
For all her playing around,

00:09:37.180 --> 00:09:39.220
that little girl is an enemy as well.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.050
She’ll trip us up if we let our guards down.

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:42.930
Kawachi-san, that’s great!

00:09:42.930 --> 00:09:44.400
Exactly.

00:09:45.230 --> 00:09:47.060
I just said the obvious thing, though...

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:48.730
All right, then,

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.400
I have to greet just one more.

00:09:52.110 --> 00:09:52.950
Let’s go.

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:57.650
Mizuno...

00:09:58.030 --> 00:09:59.280
Hello.

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:00.910
Tsukino-san, are you well?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:04.120
Hey! You shouldn’t be calling your own
older sister Tsukino-san, should you?

00:10:04.120 --> 00:10:05.080
Older sister?

00:10:06.920 --> 00:10:09.460
Azusagawa Tsukino and Azusagawa Mizuno.

00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:12.550
Of course, the two of you are siblings, are you?

00:10:12.550 --> 00:10:14.590
You’re really late in noticing.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:16.340
You’re cute!

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:18.340
Don’t hug me for everything.

00:10:18.340 --> 00:10:19.430
Geez...

00:10:19.890 --> 00:10:23.930
Can’t I get you to stop sticking to my
employee for every little thing?

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.810
She’s scary, Kazu-kun.

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:27.430
Kazu-kun?

00:10:28.520 --> 00:10:30.990
By doing something like that,
my employee will again be...

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.940
You thieving cat.

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:35.940
Thieving cat?

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:38.200
Isn’t that your mother?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:45.910
Stop, Tsukino!

00:10:47.500 --> 00:10:48.660
That hurt!

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:53.920
No way! I-I’m sorry. I...

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:56.380
Tsukino, you idiot!

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:57.880
Siblings should get along well together!

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:08.850
She got scolded!

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:11.700
Return to your station, Mizuno.

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.910
This is a good opportunity.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:21.570
There’s something I’d like to tell you.

00:11:21.570 --> 00:11:23.120
Come with me.

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:37.050
Their mothers are different!

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.510
Tsukino’s and Mizuno’s?

00:11:38.510 --> 00:11:41.720
Is that so...? Then, they’re just strangers to each other, aren’t they?

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:42.550
Are you an idiot?

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:45.560
It means that their father is the same,
and their mothers are different.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:48.140
Old man Azusagawa’s son Sadamichi had a woman

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.690
other than his wife whom he loved.

00:11:50.690 --> 00:11:54.230
Tsukino was born of the relationship
between him and that woman.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:59.070
That is why this newcomers’ battle
holds a great significance for Tsukino.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:00.150
A great significance?

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:05.200
Old man Azusagawa has, in fact, 3 granddaughters.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:08.160
Tsukino and Mizuno. And Yukino, who’s the eldest.

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.710
These granddaughters each control
a Pantasia group branch:

00:12:11.710 --> 00:12:13.210
the Southern Tokyo Branch,

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:14.580
the New Tokyo Branch,

00:12:14.580 --> 00:12:17.790
and the Central Shinjuku Branch are
under their management, but...

00:12:18.260 --> 00:12:21.720
In reality, these three sisters are being
made to compete against each other,

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:23.880
in order to determine the future successor.

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.640
Compete?

00:12:26.970 --> 00:12:30.350
In the case of Tsukino, this competition
should be called a trial.

00:12:30.730 --> 00:12:31.980
Tsukino’s older sister,

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.440
Azusagawa Yukino, is the manager
of the Central Shinjuku Branch.

00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:39.690
Amongst the branches, it has the honor
of having the #1 sales in Japan,

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:44.460
with employees 10 times our number, that
is, 40 people. It’s the top branch.

00:12:44.910 --> 00:12:48.870
It was old man Azusagawa who recommended that she go there.

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:53.000
And Azusagawa Mizuno is Tsukino’s
younger sister, but...

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:55.580
she’s the next Representative Manager Candidate of

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:58.680
the New Tokyo Branch, which is under
the Azusagawa Grand Hotels.

00:12:59.380 --> 00:13:02.720
This New Tokyo Branch has young employees,

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:06.510
and is highly successful, as it targets young customers.

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:10.890
It employs over 30 people and is #4 in
sales out of all the branches nationally.

00:13:10.890 --> 00:13:12.470
It really is in the upper stratum.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.690
The #1 and #4 country-wide...

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:19.190
And the person who recommended Mizuno

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.530
was the President of the Azusagawa Grand Hotels,

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:24.360
and the father of the three sisters...

00:13:24.360 --> 00:13:26.200
Azusagawa Sadamichi.

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:30.910
And, as you know, Tsukino is the representative of

00:13:30.910 --> 00:13:33.000
the Southern Tokyo Branch, but...

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:34.540
there are 5 employees, and...

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:34.970
That’s enough!
there are 5 employees, and...

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:35.620
That’s enough!

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:39.460
This is like a race that’s been fixed.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:41.880
Tsukino doesn’t have a chance of winning.

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:46.380
Her own father is partial towards the youngest, Mizuno,

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:51.190
and her grandfather is partial
towards the oldest, Yukino.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:56.520
Why? Why is it that only Tsukino has
no one to push her on from behind?

00:13:57.560 --> 00:13:58.610
Kawachi...

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.530
Just because her mother’s different...

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:06.110
Wasn’t that old man acting all friendly with Tsukino?

00:14:06.110 --> 00:14:07.700
Was he just posing?!

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.160
It leaves a bad taste in the mouth.

00:14:09.160 --> 00:14:12.120
No, I don’t think that’s the case.

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:15.250
Old man Azusagawa is a good man.

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:20.130
I think that he distributes his love between
all three granddaughters equally.

00:14:20.130 --> 00:14:22.300
However, it’s a fact that within Pantasia,

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:27.510
Tsukino, who’s not a legitimate
child, is not thought of well.

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:30.470
The scheme of things ended up like this

00:14:30.470 --> 00:14:33.010
so as to avoid such critical eyes as well.

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:37.020
To sum up, the old man is quite aged now.

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:39.400
We don’t know when he’ll die...

00:14:39.860 --> 00:14:43.190
It can be said that he couldn’t help being partial to

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:45.030
the oldest, who has already graduated from college.

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:50.950
She’s in a state in which nobody
expects anything of her.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.040
But she’s always bright and living to the fullest.

00:14:55.040 --> 00:14:58.290
That’s probably her being obstinate.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:03.170
However, with only obstinacy to support your heart,

00:15:03.170 --> 00:15:05.300
you never know when you’ll just flitter away.

00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:10.680
One of the reasons I left the Main Store
and volunteered to be the manager of

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:14.510
the Southern Tokyo Branch was because
I’d hoped to reinforce that support.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:17.060
I-Is that what happened?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:19.980
I thought that you’d been driven out.

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:20.520
Hey...

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:22.940
Hey, Manager...

00:15:22.940 --> 00:15:27.610
If we were to win this
newcomers’ battle, then...

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.990
we’d also become reinforcement
for this support, wouldn’t we?

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:32.620
Of course you would.

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:35.330
If it was a competition of sales between the branches, then we’d have no chance of winning.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:39.410
However, if we were to have found the person who wins the newcomers’ battle,

00:15:39.410 --> 00:15:42.000
and were to be nurturing his growth,

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:44.500
the higher-ups would have no choice
but to acknowledge Tsukino.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:48.090
That was the main reason that Tsukino joined
the Main Branch employee examination,

00:15:48.090 --> 00:15:51.600
found the two of you, and is helping you towards

00:15:51.600 --> 00:15:53.680
the newcomers’ championship.

00:15:55.220 --> 00:15:58.320
I... called Tsukino an idiot...

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.690
I... I...

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.900
It’ll be okay if we win.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:05.440
You, too.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:08.320
In this newcomers’ battle,

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:10.780
the two of us should place
first and second.

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:11.860
Rather than being simply reinforcement,

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:15.160
it would become a pillar made of the
strongest, most precious wood.

00:16:15.160 --> 00:16:15.960
Azuma!

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:19.120
Really? Kawachi...

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:19.540
Yeah.

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.670
If so, would Tsukino forgive me?

00:16:23.670 --> 00:16:24.670
Yeah.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:27.260
I’ve decided.

00:16:28.260 --> 00:16:31.050
I’ll win the championship
for Tsukino’s sake.

00:16:31.050 --> 00:16:32.430
You moron!

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:35.180
I’ll be the champion, so you should be satisfied with being runner-up.

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:36.810
No!

00:16:36.810 --> 00:16:39.680
I’ll be the one to win the championship
for Tsukino’s sake!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:42.020
Kawachi must deal with being the runner-up!

00:16:42.480 --> 00:16:43.730
What?

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:45.560
Don’t be so selfish. You moron!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.980
Look here, you two.

00:16:50.820 --> 00:16:53.450
I’m really happy right now.

00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:58.910
Pantasia...

00:16:58.910 --> 00:17:02.160
Pantasia Southern Tokyo Branch...

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.170
There it is...

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:11.590
This is quite a poor and boring looking store, isn’t it?

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:13.760
But, oh well. I can’t be saying that about other people.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:24.600
I hope that kid’s doing well...

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:26.100
Hello!

00:17:30.360 --> 00:17:32.200
W-What is he...?

00:17:34.950 --> 00:17:36.910
H-He disappeared...

00:17:37.410 --> 00:17:38.740
Was that an afterimage?

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.990
Welcome!

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.500
W-What are you?

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.460
I’m just regular personnel.

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.380
Is that so?

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.630
I’m actually not a customer.

00:17:50.630 --> 00:17:54.630
Is there a pointy-haired boy holding
his hair back with a band like this

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.470
working at this store?

00:17:57.340 --> 00:17:59.350
Ah, you mean Azuma-kun?

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.720
If you mean him, then...

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.690
It looks like you’ll be against her
in the very first round.

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:12.820
Azuma is against Mizuno in the very first round, eh?

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:14.580
That’s quite the responsibility.

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:16.200
I’m...

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:18.200
Motohashi Yuuko?

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:21.200
I’m also against a woman, am I?

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.620
I’m in the B block.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:25.300
I can’t fight with Azuma unless I reach the finals.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:30.710
In other words, the possibility of me and
Azuma being 1st and 2nd is still possible.

00:18:30.710 --> 00:18:34.800
Also, Suwabara is in the same A block as Azuma.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:38.720
God also has given me the luxury of
not having to fight both of them.

00:18:41.310 --> 00:18:42.560
His opponent hasn’t been decided yet?

00:18:43.720 --> 00:18:45.480
Rock-paper-scissors!

00:18:45.480 --> 00:18:47.850
Once more.

00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.650
They’re still doing rock-paper-scissors.
Once more.

00:18:49.650 --> 00:18:50.900
Once more.

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:52.400
Yahoo!

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:53.360
I’ve won.

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:55.190
I can participate in the finals.

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:56.200
No way...

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:59.570
I chose C because of that idiot.
But it’s not over.

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:01.870
Did you see that?
My super-strong luck.

00:19:01.870 --> 00:19:06.500
With this luck, may my first opponent be weak...

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:08.960
I will enter that blank space, and...

00:19:09.880 --> 00:19:12.250
Who do you mean by Suwabara...

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:13.390
Don’t tell me...

00:19:15.310 --> 00:19:16.380
I sense a thirst for blood...

00:19:20.090 --> 00:19:22.010
Is it you who is to be my opponent?

00:19:22.680 --> 00:19:23.720
Scary!

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:28.310
There are people who say stupid things
like luck being a part of your skill,

00:19:28.310 --> 00:19:32.020
but don’t expect such nonsense to work with me.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.860
At this pure place of confrontation,

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.730
see what happens if you make an unsightly bread!

00:19:35.730 --> 00:19:38.480
Understand that you can no longer live.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:41.990
My... my life!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.200
Please spare my life at least.

00:19:45.200 --> 00:19:47.960
Ah... it’s no challenge, right from the very start.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.950
Hey, Azuma.

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.960
That newcomer called Koala... he’s to be looked out for.

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:56.460
Soushi
Koala

00:19:56.460 --> 00:20:00.380
He has an unusual appearance, so I’ve been
observing him since the preliminaries,

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.970
but he carries himself in a way that makes
it hard to believe he’s a newcomer.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:05.640
That’s a newcomer?

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:07.520
I’ve taken a fleeting glance at him,

00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:09.720
but I thought he was Pantasia’s mascot.

00:20:09.720 --> 00:20:12.600
He’s cute, isn’t he? My Koala-chan.

00:20:13.440 --> 00:20:14.770
Azusagawa Mizuno!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:15.690
Yup!

00:20:16.030 --> 00:20:17.740
My koala, you say?

00:20:17.740 --> 00:20:20.570
He’s dressed as a koala for a reason,

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.700
but he’s a newcomer in the same branch as me.

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:24.280
What have you come for?

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.160
That’s quite the greeting, isn’t it?

00:20:26.160 --> 00:20:29.540
We’re against each other in the first round,
and are therefore rivals, so to speak.

00:20:30.460 --> 00:20:31.540
Don’t touch me!

00:20:31.540 --> 00:20:33.040
Someone like you is not a rival!

00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:35.050
Azuma-san...

00:20:35.670 --> 00:20:38.040
I seem to be quite hated, aren’t I?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.840
I don’t know what that sneaky woman

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:43.300
may have whispered to you,

00:20:43.300 --> 00:20:45.510
but she’s the one who’s
in the wrong, okay?

00:20:45.510 --> 00:20:47.600
Don’t talk like that!

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.010
Tsukino is your older sister, isn’t she?

00:20:49.010 --> 00:20:51.020
Calm down, Azuma.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:53.530
Call her nee-chan. Nee-chan!
Note: Nee-chan means older sister, and is how people refer to their older sisters in Japan.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.320
To those who are taking the finals,

00:20:57.320 --> 00:21:00.280
melon bread has been decided
to be the theme for the finals.

00:21:01.150 --> 00:21:03.200
Any special ingredients should be prepared individually.

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:06.030
And gather at noon tomorrow for the finals.

00:21:06.030 --> 00:21:06.780
That is all.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:08.160
Lucky!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.240
It’s the topic that I’m best at.

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:15.130
Well, I think that it’s impossible
to win against me at this topic,

00:21:15.130 --> 00:21:17.170
but Kazu-kun, hang in there to the end, okay?

00:21:17.500 --> 00:21:18.460
Wait!

00:21:18.460 --> 00:21:19.500
Promise me one thing.

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:21.250
Promise?

00:21:21.670 --> 00:21:24.760
If I win,
call Tsukino nee-chan as you should.

00:21:24.760 --> 00:21:26.510
Azuma-san...

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:30.560
Huh? Why should I do something like that?

00:21:30.560 --> 00:21:31.350
Moreover...

00:21:33.350 --> 00:21:34.150
Wait a minute...

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:38.440
That’s okay. I’ll do it.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:42.700
In exchange... if Kazu-kun loses,

00:21:42.700 --> 00:21:45.200
I’ll have you come over to the New
Tokyo Branch as an employee.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:46.820
W-What?

00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:49.120
Please wait one moment!

00:21:49.120 --> 00:21:50.910
Something unreasonable like that...

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:53.040
You’re the one who started it, right?

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:55.580
Or is it that you don’t have confidence in Kazu-kun?

00:21:55.580 --> 00:21:56.750
Don’t talk nonsense.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:58.040
I won’t lose to someone like you.

00:21:58.040 --> 00:22:00.130
Then, it’s a promise.

00:22:00.130 --> 00:22:01.420
All right, then.

00:22:01.420 --> 00:22:02.800
It’s a promise.

00:22:02.800 --> 00:22:04.260
Hey, Azuma!

00:22:04.590 --> 00:22:07.640
I’ll have you keep your promise at all costs, okay?

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:08.720
Bye bye...

00:22:14.350 --> 00:22:17.730
Azuma, don’t decide things so easily.

00:22:17.730 --> 00:22:20.110
Even though you don’t know anything about her skill...

00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:22.320
Moreover, are you especially good
at making melon bread?

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:25.700
Hmm... I’m bad at it...

00:22:26.450 --> 00:22:28.070
What do you mean, you’re bad at it?

00:22:39.530 --> 00:22:47.670
If I think of you, and even utter the clichéd phrase “I love you,”

00:22:48.240 --> 00:22:56.680
it makes such a nice sound, and you continue talking.

00:23:00.250 --> 00:23:07.690
The hopeless tears your bold self sometimes shows me form flag of truce.

00:23:08.990 --> 00:23:12.860
If nothing is said, then all the more,

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:19.000
I just can’t look away. Things like sadness and pain...

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:21.570
Well, that happens a lot in life, after all.

00:23:21.800 --> 00:23:25.710
When you casually say, “Do your best,” it gives me strength.

00:23:26.150 --> 00:23:30.480
Whenever your small back trembles, I will embrace you right away.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:34.320
Even if the scenery outside my window changes...

00:23:34.810 --> 00:23:39.020
Stay with me as you are, bad sleeping habits and all.

00:23:39.650 --> 00:23:44.190
If you sulk, and utter

00:23:44.460 --> 00:23:53.000
Even the clichéd “I hate you,” it comes across as the opposite.

00:23:53.400 --> 00:24:02.360
I will love you, no matter what. It’s just another Sunday to me.

00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:09.710
The topic for the first round of
the finals is... Melon Bread!

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:13.180
I don’t know what your <i>Japan</i> is,
but it won’t work against me.

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:15.510
Kazu-kun, try your hardest, okay?

00:24:15.510 --> 00:24:17.050
Next time, on Yakitate!! Japan.

00:24:17.050 --> 00:24:19.810
Sorry for the wait!!
High on Melon Bread!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:21.010
Be sure to see it!

00:24:21.310 --> 00:24:23.760
Yakitate!! Seed of knowledge.

00:24:24.060 --> 00:24:26.320
The root of the word “margarine” comes
from the Greek word for “pearl.”

00:24:26.320 --> 00:24:28.160
It is named so because during the synthesis process,

00:24:28.160 --> 00:24:30.570
the droplets of oil look like beautiful pearls.

00:24:30.570 --> 00:24:32.740
It was given this name by a French
chemist named Hippolyte.
